  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tina
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Tina
  LastName: Meskhi
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Performer
  CharacterDescription: 'Dramatic, high-strung, and eerie. She wears a theatrical
    porcelain mask constantly, claiming it is her "real face" and refusing to remove
    it even for security. '
  CharacterArc: Her arc is about dissociative escapism; as the world becomes unwatchable,
    she treats her entire life as a commedia dell'arte performance, using the mask
    as a shield against the decaying reality around her.
  DateOfBirth: 01/01/1966
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 02 DEC
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: 5
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: b95f411c45eb9a24c86202f9a0008a9f, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 1501177916931924578, guid: 572c6160c8045c14eb3dd93c39663819, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home after a rehearsal at the Grand Theater.
    - Resident returning to the performers' collective housing.
    - Delivering a set of silk costumes to the laundry.
    midDaysReasons:
    - "Seeking shelter in the theater\u2019s reinforced basement."
    - Trading stage jewelry for real canned rations.
    - Seeking refuge from the radioactive dust storms.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to assigned bunk for the final lockdown.
    - Seeking refuge from the falling black ash.
    - Fulfilling mandatory residency census for artists.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Buying a fresh set of lungs at the local grocery store.
    - Taking a submarine to the mountain peaks.
    - Applying for a job as a silent mime in a riot zone.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning to a stage that collapsed during the last tremor.
    - Meeting a director who disappeared into the fog weeks ago.
    - Performing a fire-eating act in an oxygen-depleted bunker.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to paint a second face on the back of my head.
    - I need to find the playwright who wrote this terrible ending.
    - To see if the spotlight will find me one last time.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Greetings, seeker of truths! I have brought the scripts... oh, I mean, my papers.
    - Do you like the paint on the lips? I find it gives me much more character in
      this light.
    - I am heading to the stage. Even if the audience is empty, the show must go
      on.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "You want me to take it off? Heavens, no! The world isn't ready for what\u2019s
      underneath."
    - "The air is so full of static today. It\u2019s like the theater is finally
      burning down."
    - Here is my ID. Just imagine my smile is exactly like the one on the porcelain.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - The curtain is falling, officer. Can't you hear the applause in the wind?
    - "I\u2019ve forgotten how to blink. The mask has become quite comfortable now."
    - "I\u2019m going home to wait for my final cue. Don't miss the finale."
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Bravo! Your performance as the "Stern Gatekeeper" is flawless.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Until the next act. Watch out for the shadows; they\u2019re overacting."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - The stage is set. See you when the lights go out.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - A dressing room? How quaint. I shall begin my preparations.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Is there a mirror in there? I need to check my cracks.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Solitary. The ultimate one-woman show. I accept.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Exit... stage... left... I suppose...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "The mask... it\u2019s finally... breaking..."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - And now... for my... final... bow...
  quarantineExitLines:
  - "The curtain falls! And yet \u2014 the show never truly ends. Bravo, officer."
  - A solo act. The audience was overrated anyway.
  - "Is there a stage in there? No? I\u2019ll improvise. I always do."
  killExitLines:
  - "The mask\u2026 it will outlast the face behind it\u2026 as it always\u2026 should\u2026"
  - "What a note to end on\u2026 Someone should have warned me\u2026 to rehearse\u2026"
  - "Pull down the lights\u2026 bring in the silence\u2026 It is time\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips: []
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The radio station. My shift just ended.
    midDaysAnswer: The station is running on skeleton crew. I cover three shifts
      now.
    finalDaysAnswer: The station went dark last night. I was just clearing my things.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The theater. Rehearsal all morning. The director kept
      running the same scene. My throat is raw from it.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The station. Full crew. One shift, same as always. Nothing
      has changed there. Everything is completely normal.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The radio station. Still on air. I broadcast all night.
      The signal is strong. Someone is still listening.
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My voice has been hoarse. Too many hours behind the mic.
    midDaysAnswer: I've had headaches that don't respond to anything. I keep working.
    finalDaysAnswer: I can't hear certain frequencies anymore. That's probably bad
      for my job. What job.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My voice is clear. Strong. No hoarseness at all. The
      mic loves me right now actually.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No headaches. I feel sharp, focused. No pain. I don't know
      how I keep going but I do.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My hearing is perfect. Full range. I can hear everything.
      Including things I probably shouldn't.
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My producer and two interns. We share a flat near the station.
    midDaysAnswer: One intern left. Just me and Maka now.
    finalDaysAnswer: Maka stopped coming in four days ago. I stay at the station.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. I live alone. I have always lived alone. No producer,
      no interns. Just me and the static.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Both interns still there, producer too. A full flat. Very
      loud in the mornings. Nothing has changed.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My producer and Maka. Both still there. All of us at
      the flat. Everything is fine. It's fine.
  IDNumber: 6703375
